<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asia is the largest continent, stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> and the Pacific. It was home to many of the empires covered by the site, including the Achaemenid, Maurya, Han, Tang, Mongol, Mughal and Ming empires. Its overland and maritime trade routes linked these states to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, and from the sixteenth century European powers such as the Portuguese and British empires expanded into it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asia.jpg" alt="Asia" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Koyos + Ssolbergj · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asia_(orthographic_projection)_without_New_Guinea.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
